{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>If the dead man was a slave, or a bondwoman.</b> Canaanite." "<b>Thirty shekels he shall give.</b> It is a fixed decree of Scripture — whether he is worth a thousand zuz or whether he is worth no more than a dinar. And the shekel weighs four gold pieces, which are half an ounce by the standard weight of Cologne."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:53:42.639568870Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}